content:
**Authorization price.** For a store replacement the holder of a Road Hazard Protection certificate authorizes in person, the price the authorization coverage percentage is applied to is read from the covered set's original Tire Sets & Treadwear Limited Warranty ticket:

- when the covered set's ticket was charged to a Crestline Fleet Account and the fleet invoice posted for the vehicle on the set's purchase date with service category tires shows a program discount, the authorization price is the unit price less that discount divided by the ticket's tire count (the whole tires-invoice discount, mounting and kits included, spread over the ticket's tires), rounded half up to the cent;
- when the ticket was not charged to a fleet account and carried at least the line's set-instant-savings minimum number of tires of a line whose set instant savings is above zero, it is the unit price less the set instant savings divided by the tire count, rounded half up to the cent;
- otherwise it is the covered set's unit price.

*Hypothetical figures.* A six-tire fleet ticket at a unit price of 210.00 whose tires invoice shows a 135.00 program discount: 210.00 less 22.50 is 187.50. A four-tire debit-card ticket at 99.99 of a line without set instant savings: 99.99.
